{"meta":{"dataset":"evictions","title":"Eviction filings by county and year (LSC Civil Court Data Initiative)","version":"1.0.0","doi":"10.5281/zenodo.23752996","doiUrl":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23752996","conceptDoi":"10.5281/zenodo.23752995","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","attribution":"Source: Probative, Eviction filings by county and year (LSC Civil Court Data Initiative), version 1.0.0, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23752996, licensed CC BY 4.0.","citation":"Probative. (2026). Eviction filings by county and year (LSC Civil Court Data Initiative) (Version 1.0.0) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23752996","disclaimer":"Not legal advice. These are counts of eviction cases filed in court, kept for research and market sizing. A filing is not an eviction carried out, a finding against a tenant or a measure of need, and one household can be filed against more than once. Questions about an eviction are for a licensed attorney or a local legal aid office.","notice":"Probative is a marketing firm, not a law firm; not legal advice.","lastChecked":"2026-10-29","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/index.json","humanUrl":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/evictions/","statusCodes":{"P":"primary source","S":"secondary source","D":"ABA model default","U":"open question"}},"summary":"Eviction filings (cases) by county and month from the Legal Services Corporation's Civil Court Data Initiative Eviction Tracker, which collects residential eviction filings from state and local courts: 1,464 counties and 34 states and territories, January 2016 through September 2025. Each record carries the filings of every full calendar year the county reports, the last twelve months where all twelve are present, filings per 100 renter households, the poverty rate and the latest month against the county's own historical average. Counties carry the Census FIPS code. LSC's data are released under CC0 1.0. The states and territories in the file are the ones LSC reports; the US record totals a year or month only where every one of them reports it.","key":"jurisdiction","count":1499,"keys":[{"key":"AK","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/AK.json","records":29},{"key":"AR","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/AR.json","records":76},{"key":"AZ","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/AZ.json","records":3},{"key":"CO","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/CO.json","records":63},{"key":"CT","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/CT.json","records":9},{"key":"DE","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/DE.json","records":4},{"key":"FL","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/FL.json","records":43},{"key":"GA","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/GA.json","records":4},{"key":"HI","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/HI.json","records":5},{"key":"ID","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/ID.json","records":44},{"key":"IN","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/IN.json","records":93},{"key":"KS","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/KS.json","records":2},{"key":"KY","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/KY.json","records":121},{"key":"ME","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/ME.json","records":17},{"key":"MN","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/MN.json","records":88},{"key":"MS","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/MS.json","records":2},{"key":"MT","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/MT.json","records":36},{"key":"NC","url":"https://probativegrowth.com/data/v1/evictions/jurisdictions/NC.json","